### Try the API from VS Code (install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request").
### Start the API first:  uvicorn api.main:app --reload     (and train once:  python -m src.train)

### Is the service alive and the model loaded?
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/health

### Which model is deployed and how did it do on the held-out test patients?
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/model-info

### The 30 feature names the model expects
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/features

### A held-out example patient (add ?malignant=true for a malignant one). Copy the JSON it returns.
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/sample?malignant=true

### Score one patient: paste the JSON from /sample as the body (the "id" and "actual" keys are ignored)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/predict?threshold=0.5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "features": {
    "radius_mean": 17.99, "texture_mean": 10.38, "perimeter_mean": 122.8, "area_mean": 1001.0,
    "smoothness_mean": 0.1184, "compactness_mean": 0.2776, "concavity_mean": 0.3001, "concave points_mean": 0.1471,
    "symmetry_mean": 0.2419, "fractal_dimension_mean": 0.07871,
    "radius_se": 1.095, "texture_se": 0.9053, "perimeter_se": 8.589, "area_se": 153.4,
    "smoothness_se": 0.006399, "compactness_se": 0.04904, "concavity_se": 0.05373, "concave points_se": 0.01587,
    "symmetry_se": 0.03003, "fractal_dimension_se": 0.006193,
    "radius_worst": 25.38, "texture_worst": 17.33, "perimeter_worst": 184.6, "area_worst": 2019.0,
    "smoothness_worst": 0.1622, "compactness_worst": 0.6656, "concavity_worst": 0.7119, "concave points_worst": 0.2654,
    "symmetry_worst": 0.4601, "fractal_dimension_worst": 0.1189
  }
}
